{
    "name": "search_result",
    "package": "@wexample/symfony-search",
    "type": "class",
    "description": "One thing found, whatever kind of thing it is.\nAn entity without an ORM mapping. Nothing is ever persisted from here — the\nrow it points at already exists, and a page points at no row at all. It is an\nentity for what being one gives on the way out: the pseudocode export, the\ngenerated `SearchResult.ts` and its repository, and a collection of results\nbeing a collection of entities like any other, which the front already knows\nhow to render. Doctrine skips a class carrying no `#[ORM\\Entity]`, so\nextending `AbstractEntity` costs nothing but the identity it brings.\nThat is also why the `Has*Trait` of symfony-helpers are not used here: they\ncarry `#[Column]`, and a column is exactly what none of these fields has.",
    "properties": [
        {
            "name": "id",
            "type": "Symfony\\Component\\Uid\\Uuid"
        },
        {
            "name": "type",
            "type": "string"
